  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing self-deprecation",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'this isn't even my final form', which uses the first-person pronoun 'my' to create a self-referential joke. The user identifies with the cosplayers' perspective, imagining themselves as the characters and humorously claiming their current form is not even close to their ultimate power state. This projection is onto the textual material, which explicitly uses 'my' to anchor the humor to the viewer's imagined identity as the character.",
